Reads the manifest and every listed object of the connection, and checks size, checksum, the content of
each document, and that every flag-set source resolves. It never writes. Exit code 5 when a problem is found.

Usage:
  semaphore-cli publish verify [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help[=true|false]   help for verify

Global Flags:
      --bucket string         bucket (without --config)
      --channel string        channel of the manifest (without --config; default stable)
  -c, --config string         bootstrap file whose controlPlane connection is the target
      --connection string     connection name written in the manifest (without --config; default control)
      --endpoint string       S3 endpoint, for emulators and S3 compatible stores (without --config)
      --manifest-key string   manifest key (without --config; default <prefix>manifests/<channel>.yaml)
  -o, --output string         output format: text or json (default "text")
      --prefix string         key prefix of the objects and of the default manifest key
      --region string         AWS region (without --config)
